@startuml
title TripPublished with outbox and inbox

actor Driver
participant "ShareTrip API" as API
participant "Trip Application Service" as TripService
database "Trip DB" as TripDB
participant "Outbox Publisher" as Publisher
queue "Kafka: trip.events" as Kafka
participant "Notification Service" as Notification
database "Notification DB" as NotificationDB

Driver -> API: POST /trip/publish {tripId}
API -> TripService: PublishTrip(ctx, PublishTripCommand)
TripService -> TripDB: BEGIN; load trip FOR UPDATE
TripDB --> TripService: Trip
TripService -> TripService: Check DriverID = ClientID and status = draft
TripService -> TripDB: Save published + history + outbox_events (TripPublished)
TripService -> TripDB: COMMIT
TripDB --> TripService: committed

TripService --> API: tripId
API --> Driver: 200 {tripId}

loop every second
  Publisher -> TripDB: BEGIN
  Publisher -> TripDB: SELECT pending ORDER BY created_at\nLIMIT 100 FOR UPDATE SKIP LOCKED
  TripDB --> Publisher: outbox events
  loop each event
    Publisher -> Kafka: PublishTripPublished(key=trip_id)
    note over Publisher, Kafka
      event_id=outbox_events.id, event_type=TripPublished, trip_id,
      driver_id=ClientID, company_id=ClientID, occurred_at
    end note
    Kafka --> Publisher: ack (RequiredAcks=all)
    Publisher -> TripDB: UPDATE status='sent', sent_at=now()
  end
  Publisher -> TripDB: COMMIT
end

Notification -> Kafka: FetchMessage(group=notification-service)
Kafka --> Notification: TripPublished
Notification -> Notification: HandleTripPublished(ctx, event)
Notification -> NotificationDB: BEGIN
Notification -> NotificationDB: INSERT processed_events(event_id)\nON CONFLICT DO NOTHING
alt new event_id
  NotificationDB --> Notification: inserted
  Notification -> NotificationDB: INSERT notification\nrecipient_id=driver_id, type=trip_published\nstatus=created, payload=event
else event_id already processed
  NotificationDB --> Notification: duplicate; skip notification
end
Notification -> NotificationDB: COMMIT
NotificationDB --> Notification: committed
Notification -> Kafka: CommitMessages(offset)

note over Notification, NotificationDB
  On a database error: ROLLBACK and no offset commit.
  Kafka can deliver an uncommitted event again after restart.
end note
@enduml
